Package: dgen
Type: Package
Title: Data Generator for Statistical Teaching and Testing
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Todd", "Daniel", email = "ToddDaniel@missouristate.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Brendan", "Morse", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Author of the original MorseGen functions (stat.gen, cor.gen), 1982-2018, on which this package's design is based")
    )
Description: Generates datasets with exact statistical properties—means,
    standard deviations, and correlations—for teaching statistics and
    validating analytical workflows. Uses iterative refinement to achieve
    specified parameters rather than approximations. Supports t-tests
    (one-sample, independent, paired), ANOVA (one-way, two-way, blocked),
    chi-square tests (goodness-of-fit, independence), proportion tests,
    linear and logistic regression, and psychometric scales. Each function
    generates data and automatically runs the corresponding analysis,
    returning results alongside effect sizes and assumption checks.
